# Rust build output
/target/
crates/*/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# uv-managed Python env (built by `uv sync`; .dspy-venv* are older spellings).
# Without the second spelling a *symlink* named `.venv` — which is how a worktree borrows the
# main checkout's env — is not matched by the trailing slash, and `git add -A` commits a link
# to an absolute path nobody else has.
.venv/
.venv
.dspy-venv*/
.dspy-venv*

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.*
*.local

# Local-only comparison against other projects (never tracked)
/local-compare/

# cargo-mutants scratch trees and logs
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# The internal working notes: the plan and the handoff. Kept on a developer's machine, out of the
# repository — a reader of this project should meet it through README.md and docs/, and neither of
# these had stayed true enough to publish. What they carry that *is* published — the observed test
# counts — lives in `scripts/status.toml`, which is tracked, so nothing a reader sees goes stale
# because a note nobody could see went stale.
/backlog.toml
/HANDOFF.md
